<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50922" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĭgōro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a. and n.
		vigor. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to animate</i>, <i>invigorate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">disciplinam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pud. 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juvenis vigoratus,</span>”
				<i>stout</i>, <i>lusty</i>, <i>vigorous</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 227</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to become strong</i>,
				<i>gain strength</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum animae vigorantis ex vite Christi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Res. Carn. 26 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
